            <div class="theorem-header-section">
                <h2 class="theorem-title tex2jax_process">
                   Vanishing Implies First Jet Separation (Theorem # 9108)
                </h2>
            </div>

            <div class="theorem-section">
                
                
                    <div class="theorem-box">
                        <div class="theorem-box-header">
                            <span class="theorem-label">Theorem</span>
                            
                            <div class="theorem-header-actions">
                              <a href="/theorems/9108/edit" class="view-tags-btn">Edit</a>
                              <a href="/theorems/9108/code" class="view-tags-btn">Code</a>
                              <a href="/theorems/9108/issues" class="view-tags-btn">Issues</a>
                              <a href="/theorems/9108/pull-requests" class="view-tags-btn">Pull Requests</a>
                              <a href="/theorems/9108/attributions" class="view-tags-btn">Attributions</a>
                              <a href="/theorems/9108/admin" class="view-tags-btn">Admin</a>
                            </div>
                            
                        </div>
                        
                        
                        <div class="content-renderer content-text"
                             data-renderer-id="theorem-statement-renderer"
                             data-binding-context-base64="eyJ2ZXJzaW9uIjoxLCJiaW5kaW5ncyI6W10sInRoZW9yZW1faWQiOjkxMDgsInNvdXJjZV9oYXNoIjoiMTYyNjIzNmU2YzIxOTA0Y2UyMWNiZDAxOWFlY2VkY2YiLCJzb3VyY2Vfa2luZCI6InRoZW9yZW0tc3RhdGVtZW50In0="
                             data-binding-context-mode="source">
                            
                              <div class="raw-markdown-content" style="display: none;">Let $X$ be a complex manifold of complex dimension $n$, let $M \to X$ be a holomorphic line bundle, and write $M$ also for its sheaf of holomorphic sections. Let $x \in X$, let $|M|$ denote the complete linear system associated to $M$, and let $\mathcal I_x \subset \mathcal O_X$ denote the ideal sheaf of holomorphic functions vanishing at $x$. If
\begin{align*}
H^1(X,M\otimes_{\mathcal O_X}\mathcal I_x^2)=0,
\end{align*}
then $M$, equivalently $|M|$, separates first jets at $x$: the first-jet evaluation map
\begin{align*}
j_x^1:H^0(X,M)\longrightarrow H^0(X,M\otimes_{\mathcal O_X}\mathcal O_X/\mathcal I_x^2)
\end{align*}
induced by the quotient morphism $\mathcal O_X \to \mathcal O_X/\mathcal I_x^2$ is surjective. Equivalently, after choosing any holomorphic coordinate chart centered at $x$ and any holomorphic local frame of $M$ near $x$, every prescribed constant term and $n$ first partial derivatives of the local expression of a section of $M$ at $x$ is realised by a global holomorphic section of $M$.</div>
                              <div class="rendered-markdown-content"></div>
                            
                        </div>
                        

